---
description: Keep diffs small; match file style; do not clean up unrelated code
alwaysApply: true
---

# Surgical Changes

Diffs must be as small as possible. Every extra line is a bug risk and a review cost.

- Do not touch code you were not asked to touch (renames, comment typos, import order).
- Match the file: quotes, naming, semicolons, even `var` if that is what the file uses.
- Clean up only what your change made unused. Pre-existing dead code stays unless asked.
- Do not reformat, prettier, or reindent unrelated lines.

Test: can every changed line be justified by the request? If a line is "while I was in there", revert it.
